Here's my gut reaction: Option A (just calories) would genuinely make me pause and think once or twice a month. Options B and C with the warnings feel like background noise – everyone knows chocolate isn't exactly a health food, so telling me it causes cancer is just stating the obvious in a preachy way. C with the actual gore photos would honestly put me off the whole vending machine experience. D and E without any calorie info are useless to me because I actually do want to know what I'm consuming. F, nothing changes.

